WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
Speaker 1: The legal problems for conspiracy&nbsp;
theorist Alex Jones and four former Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:15.680
associate Roger Stone continue. And you might&nbsp;
remember that on the one hand, Roger Stone was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:21.600
convicted and subsequently pardoned, but he&nbsp;
had has had his fair share of legal trouble.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:28.160
Alex Jones is in the middle of multiple lawsuits,&nbsp;
including some related to his conspiracy theories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.760
and false claims of a false flag in the context&nbsp;
of the Sandy Hook shooting back in 2012.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.960
And they both now have even more legal troubles.&nbsp;
Alex Jones and Roger Stone have been subpoenaed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:47.680
the House panel investigating the Jan. six riots.&nbsp;
The panel said it subpoenaed Trump spokesman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.280
Taylor Budda, which Republican political operative&nbsp;
Roger Stone and conspiracy monger Alex Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.480
as well as two others in a report by CNBC.&nbsp;
The House panel says the new recipients,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.640
who have been asked for testimony and documents,&nbsp;
are believed to have knowledge of the plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:10.800
and funding for the rallies on January 6th. Now&nbsp;
we're going to see whether they actually respond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.760
to these subpoenas or whether they will end up&nbsp;
being held in contempt. But these are clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:24.480
key figures, and there's a few different things to&nbsp;
think about Alex. Steve Bannon has also now been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.840
indicted for his ignoring of a subpoena from this&nbsp;
committee, so a few different things. Number one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:36.240
it really seems like Alex Jones is an important&nbsp;
figure in the Jan. six Trump riots the day before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.880
the riots. There's a video that was posted to his&nbsp;
website Infowars.com, which shows him telling a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:50.720
crowd in Freedom Plaza in Washington, D.C. We have&nbsp;
only begun to resist the globalists or globalists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:56.400
as he says. We have only begun to fight against&nbsp;
tyranny. They have tried to steal this election&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.520
in front of everyone. I don't know how this is all&nbsp;
going to end, he said. But if they want to fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:09.040
they better believe they've got one. That was&nbsp;
the night before the Jan. six riots. This guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:14.000
seems to be up to his eyeballs involved in&nbsp;
this thing, and he has now been subpoenaed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.520
Roger Stone has now been subpoenaed. Trump&nbsp;
spokesman Taylor Budo, which has been subpoenaed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.000
and of course, Stephen Bannon, ignored his&nbsp;
subpoena and has now been indicted for that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.880
Will we ever really learn the full scope of&nbsp;
the planning that the preplanning that went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.280
on? I don't know if we will. I really don't.&nbsp;
But it's pretty clear that these guys are up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.880
to their eyeballs in the stuff, and the Jan. six&nbsp;
committee should keep going and going and going.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:43.760
There may not be political consequences. In fact,&nbsp;
unfortunately, I think there probably will not be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:52.800
The elected officials who were involved&nbsp;
are mostly in safe red districts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.840
in safe red states or not even up for reelection&nbsp;
when it comes to senators in the immediate future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.280
And they will most likely all get reelected&nbsp;
and there probably won't be legal consequences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.880
for them. But when it comes to people like Alex&nbsp;
Jones, whoever they can get, they should pursue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.480
if that's where the evidence points. And that&nbsp;
is absolutely where the evidence is pointing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.560
right now. So continued legal trouble for Alex&nbsp;
Jones and others, and we'll see what comes of it.

